<div style="color:#111111;" class="rounded p-6 gap-3 bg-light text-dark" data-zesty-id="content:wysiwyg_basic:7:93"><div class="btgrid">
	<div class="row row-1">
		<div class="col-lg-6 col-md-12 col-sm-12">
			<div class="content">
				<p style="text-align:center;">
					<img src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/uss-cache.salvationarmy.org/719503a5-b507-4962-a44c-99d5812e42ce_shield-girl.png" style="display:block;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;" class="d-block mx-auto img-fluid rounded">
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="col-lg-6 col-md-12 col-sm-12">
			<div class="content">
				<h5 style="text-align:center;">Who Can Join?</h5>

				<p>
					Any man between the ages of 21 – 62 years of age. He must have a social security card and picture identification.
				</p>

				<p>
					Every potential participant undergoes a comprehensive intake interview to ensure the arc program is the best possible match for them. If the interview process determines it’s not, we’ll make every effort to refer them to a program that will be.
				</p>

				<p>
					A long–term commitment of at least six months is required so patterns of poor decision–making can be broken and replaced with positive life choices, changes that will help them become productive citizens of their community.
				</p>

				<p>
					Applicants with a desire to get help may be referred by families, friends, courts, clergy and community leaders, or may simply call the Intake Office at <a href="tel:504-835-7130" target="">504-835-7130</a> to make an appointment or get more information about our local ARC program.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div></div>
<div class="py-5" data-zesty-id="design:design:whitespace-xl:8:2"></div>
